<div><span class="lens-idx">01 · Ostinato</span><h2 class="lens-title">Repetition as a ground</h2></div>
</div>
<p class="lens-idea"><strong>The musical idea:</strong> An ostinato is a short rhythmic, melodic, or harmonic pattern that repeats persistently.</p>
<p class="lens-builds"><strong>How it functions:</strong> The repetition creates continuity and accumulating force while other layers enter, change, or pull attention elsewhere.</p>
<p class="lens-q"><em>What keeps returning while the rest of the music changes?</em></p>
<p class="lens-cue">First hear the low pattern alone. Then follow that same pattern beneath a changing upper line.</p>
<div class="realmusic viz-embed">
<div class="realmusic-head"><span class="rm-tag">Isolate the element</span><span class="rm-work">Ground alone · ground beneath a changing upper line</span></div>
<p class="rm-intro">The first example presents the low eight-note pattern by itself. The second keeps that pattern in place while a higher line enters and changes above it. Listen for persistence under change: the ostinato remains identifiable even when it is no longer the only event.</p>
