<p class="rm-intro">Stravinsky keeps a persistent stamped field in place while displaced reeds, low grounding, and brass pressure points enter at competing moments. Their changing alignment makes rhythm itself a compositional process: the passage grows through entry, density, displacement, and collision.</p>
